===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|non|Svalbarð|g=n}} probably through Norwegian. From {{compound|non|svalr|barð|t1=cool|t2=edge, brim|nocat=1}}, thus roughly meaning {{mention-gloss|cold shore}}, probably alluding to the treeless landscape mostly covered with grass.

The name was first attested in annales referring to year 1194, but it’s uncertain whether it referred to the modern archipelago. <ref>{{cite-book|year=2020|author=L. Chekin|title=Svalbarðs fundr : The Place Name Svalbard and Its Connotations in Medieval and Modern Literature and Cartography|doi=https://doi.org/10.7557/13.5025}}</ref> <ref>{{cite-book|year=1925|author=R. Hennig|title=Von rätselhaften Ländern : Versunkene Stätten der Geschichte}}</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|fo|Svalbarð}}, {{cog|is|Svalbarði}} and {{cog|no|-}} {{m|nn|Svalbard}}.

